base/
!base/*.json
override/
# ⚠️⚠️ `repo/` USED TO BE IGNORED WHOLESALE, AND THAT HID THE ENTIRE SERVER-SIDE LUA FROM THIS REPO.
# repo/quests is now TRACKED HERE so a clone of Twochords/AoTv4 brings the quests the live server
# actually runs. It was a nested git clone of ProjectEQ/projecteqquests; its .git was moved to
# /src/repo_backups/quests_dotgit (and bundled) so the tree could be stored as FILES -- git records a
# directory containing .git as a bare commit SHA, which clones as an EMPTY directory and silently
# delivers nothing.
# 📌 Consequence: `git pull` from ProjectEQ upstream no longer applies to this tree. It is heavily
# customised and was never pulled from them, so that is the intended trade.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE DLL SOURCE IS NOW TRACKED HERE TOO (2026-08-20), on the condition this note set out:
# the build cache is ignored FIRST. The tree is 392MB but only 3.8MB of that is source (198 files);
# the rest is .vs/ (300MB, incl. a 145MB EQGAME.ipch) and src/Release/ (66MB). GitHub hard-fails any
# file over 100MB, so those MUST stay ignored -- staging them does not make a large push, it makes a
# REJECTED one. Its nested .git was moved to /src/repo_backups/eqcoredll_dotgit and bundled at
# /src/repo_backups/eqcoredll_20260820.bundle; the history also lives on Twochords/Dinput.
# 📌 WHY: it was ignored on the grounds that the server never reads it, which is true and was the
# wrong test. `git status` in /src then said nothing about it, and three whole features
# (core_difficulty, core_fellowship, core_travel) sat untracked in a container for weeks -- the exact
# failure this file's FIRST paragraph records for the Lua. What matters is whether losing the
# container loses the work, not whether the server parses it.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ `repo/` HOLDS FOUR TREES, NOT TWO -- IGNORE BY EXCEPTION, NEVER BY REMOVING THE RULE.
# Un-ignoring `repo/` wholesale exposes 3.6GB, including TWO files past GitHub's 100MB hard limit:
#     repo/maps/master.zip                          1007MB
#     repo/eq-core-dll/.vs/.../EQGAME.ipch           139MB
# Either one turns the push into a rejection, and a 3.2GB maps tree would bloat the clone the live
# server has to pull forever. Only `repo/quests` is wanted here.
# ⚠️ Ignore the dll's BUILD OUTPUT by exception -- never the whole tree again.
repo/eq-core-dll/.vs/
repo/eq-core-dll/src/Release/
repo/eq-core-dll/src/Debug/
repo/eq-core-dll/src/x64/
repo/eq-core-dll/**/*.ipch
repo/eq-core-dll/**/Browse.VC.db
repo/eq-core-dll/**/*.VC.db
repo/maps/
repo/eqemu-definitions/
cache/
